</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span><span id="S5.T7.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-method generalization capabilities.</span> <em id="S5.T7.13" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">GAP</em> generalizes well across various pruning methods and consistently enhances performance across all tested methods. Results are reported for a fixed pruning ratio of 0.5, both with and without <em id="S5.T7.14" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">GAP</em>. The rightmost column normalizes accuracy relative to the w/o pruning baseline. Refer to <a href="#S5.SS4" title="5.4 Generalization Capabilities ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Grounding-Aware Token Pruning: Recovering from Drastic Performance Drops in Visual Grounding Caused by Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a> for further details.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further evaluate the generalization capabilities of <em id="S5.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">GAP</em>, we conducted experiments across both different pruning methods (<em id="S5.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cross-method</em>) and different token reduction ratios (<em id="S5.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cross-ratio</em>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-Method Evaluation.</span>
We applied <em id="S5.SS4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">GAP</em> to multiple pruning methods to assess its effectiveness beyond the primary methods used in the main results. The evaluated methods include:</p>
<ul id="S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CLS-visual pruning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite> (pruning method in <a href="#S5.T5" title="In 5.2 Main Results ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Grounding-Aware Token Pruning: Recovering from Drastic Performance Drops in Visual Grounding Caused by Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Text-visual pruning (<a href="#S5.E5" title="In 5.1 Evaluation Setup ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Grounding-Aware Token Pruning: Recovering from Drastic Performance Drops in Visual Grounding Caused by Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Random pruning (<a href="#S5.E6" title="In 5.1 Evaluation Setup ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Grounding-Aware Token Pruning: Recovering from Drastic Performance Drops in Visual Grounding Caused by Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Spatial pruning (<a href="#S5.E7" title="In 5.1 Evaluation Setup ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Grounding-Aware Token Pruning: Recovering from Drastic Performance Drops in Visual Grounding Caused by Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-Ratio Evaluation.</span>
Beyond different pruning methods, we also examined the effectiveness of <em id="S5.SS4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">GAP</em> across varying pruning reduction ratios. While the primary results were reported with a fixed ratio of 0.5, we extended the evaluation to ratios ranging from 0.2 to 0.8 to determine whether the impact of <em id="S5.SS4.p3.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">GAP</em> remains consistent across different levels of token pruning. These results further validate the robustness of <em id="S5.SS4.p3.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">GAP</em> across a broad range of pruning settings.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in <a href="#S5.T7" title="In 5.4 Generalization Capabilities ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Grounding-Aware Token Pruning: Recovering from Drastic Performance Drops in Visual Grounding Caused by Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and <a href="#S5.F4" title="In 5.4 Generalization Capabilities ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Grounding-Aware Token Pruning: Recovering from Drastic Performance Drops in Visual Grounding Caused by Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, the performance drop is consistent across different pruning methods and reduction ratios. More importantly, <em id="S5.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">GAP</em> consistently recovers performance across all settings, demonstrating its effectiveness in mitigating pruning-induced degradation regardless of the pruning strategy or token reduction severity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">One key observation from <a href="#S5.F4" title="In 5.4 Generalization Capabilities ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Grounding-Aware Token Pruning: Recovering from Drastic Performance Drops in Visual Grounding Caused by Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is that when the pruning ratio is around 75% to 90%, the accuracy surpasses the baseline. This aligns with findings in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>, suggesting that a slight reduction in tokens can sometimes enhance performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2506.21873v1/img/fig_ratio_ver2.png" id="S5.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/544;" width="685" height="544" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S5.F4.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Cross-ratio generalization capabilities.<span id="S5.F4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The gray line represents the w/o pruning result with 100% tokens. This figure shows the accuracy trend across different pruning ratios using the CLS-visual pruning method <a href="#S5.E4" title="In 5.1 Evaluation Setup ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Grounding-Aware Token Pruning: Recovering from Drastic Performance Drops in Visual Grounding Caused by Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, with and without <em id="S5.F4.6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">GAP</em>. See <a href="#S5.SS4" title="5.4 Generalization Capabilities ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Grounding-Aware Token Pruning: Recovering from Drastic Performance Drops in Visual Grounding Caused by Pruning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a> for more details.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.5 </span>Checking Visual Question Answering Results</h3>

<figure id="S5.T8" class="ltx_table">
